			<div class="content" id="post-content-3635190">
									

<p>-1</p>
<p>I found the description to be confusing, clunky, and somewhat unsubstantiated. It feels like the whole thing was really a set up for the Conga event, though I will admit the mental image there was VERY amusing!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>You're not really being scientific or clinical with this document. For instance, how, exactly, do we know that these things are sapient? How do we even know that they are entities if there's no way to see/measure them? It sounds like you're taking the word of the people &quot;possessed,&quot; in which case it could very well be memetic.</p>
<p>We only know of two instances, but you claim that during a &quot;New Yorker&quot; event, they will split in two. So I guess this only happened once, and we're assuming it happens every time? Then you claim the instances &quot;accelerate&quot; away from -C. Like how do we know where they're going, what they're doing if we can't see or track them? How do we even know where they went, or what they did?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-3119 retains its 'Safe' classification because the rate of this exponential growth is slow, and the current number of instances is easy to contain.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yeah, no, this really needs to be at least Euclid. Things far easier to contain are Euclid.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I want to put down in writing Hannah's dedication to the Foundation during the fire two months ago. In taking that conga line into a burning building she showed both leadership and guts. — Researcher M. Dantzler</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What does that even mean? It sounds like you're trying to mix amusing/solemn here, but to me it's just confusing. Why did Hannah Conga into a burning building? Was she trying to neutralize the anomaly? SCP doesn't do that. Why did everyone ELSE follow her? Maybe you meant to say that she Conga'd OUT of the burning building?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

