			<div class="content" id="post-content-3635705">
									

<p>Hmm, let me think about that.</p>
<p>A big part of the feel I want to evoke is the work environment of the Foundation, here. If I had to make up the contained classification distributions I'd write down 90% Safe, 9% Euclid, 1% Keter, if nothing else because Safe objects are easier and cheaper to secure. I want to tell an everyday story in the SCP universe, so that means I want 3119 to be Safe.</p>
<p>You mention the 0% chance of 1470 breaching. Currently the containment procedures would supply 42 hours of club dancing plus say 4 of PROCEDURE-3119-AMERICAN-SMOOTH, with only 35 being needed. The 42h would be supplied organically by the nightclubs being open and staying popular even if the Foundation forgot about it&#8230;</p>
<p>The other route I could go down is that everyone knows this should be Euclid (as has been mentioned repeatedly) and the Site Director is refusing the reclassification for reasons of (<em>workspace evoke</em>, probably funding).</p>
<p>OK, I think I see a way forward, and I'll add it in an Addendum document linked next to the object classification.</p>

